WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:06.182
Module two. Inventory. How a vendor adds stock, and how price and policy change

2
00:00:06.182 --> 00:00:07.136
Requests work.

3
00:00:09.333 --> 00:00:12.775
A vendor with an approved warehouse is ready to sell.

4
00:00:12.775 --> 00:00:16.153
But nothing is on sale until the vendor adds S K Us.

5
00:00:16.153 --> 00:00:18.101
This module shows exactly how.

6
00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:21.090
First, adding an S K U, step by step.

7
00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:26.148
Then the three price fields: M R P, selling price and G S T type.

8
00:00:26.598 --> 00:00:29.883
Then how a vendor asks for a different price, with a reason.

9
00:00:30.333 --> 00:00:33.554
Then how to ask for a different warranty or return policy.

10
00:00:34.004 --> 00:00:37.844
Then what the admin sees, and what happens on accept or reject.

11
00:00:38.294 --> 00:00:41.004
And finally, stock status, sync and export.

12
00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:46.621
Adding an S K U always follows the same six steps.

13
00:00:47.071 --> 00:00:50.463
Open Inventory, and click Add S K U on the top right.

14
00:00:50.913 --> 00:00:55.948
Filter by category. Only categories the admin approved for this vendor appear here.

15
00:00:56.398 --> 00:01:01.110
Pick the product from the master catalog. The vendor never types a product name.

16
00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:03.054
It always comes from the catalog.

17
00:01:03.504 --> 00:01:06.064
Choose the warehouse where this stock physically sits.

18
00:01:06.514 --> 00:01:09.501
Enter the stock quantity, and the minimum order quantity.

19
00:01:09.951 --> 00:01:14.537
Review price and policy, set cash on delivery, and click Create S K U.

20
00:01:16.933 --> 00:01:18.853
Let's watch this in the live demo.

21
00:01:21.867 --> 00:01:25.174
Here is the live demo. The vendor opens Inventory.

22
00:01:32.267 --> 00:01:36.918
The inventory page lists every S K U. The vendor clicks Add S K U.

23
00:01:44.267 --> 00:01:49.417
First, filter by category. Cement, steel, paint and tiles are the categories

24
00:01:49.417 --> 00:01:52.331
Approved for this vendor. Cement is chosen.

25
00:01:56.267 --> 00:02:02.027
Then the product, from the master catalog: J K Super Protect Cement, fifty kilo bag.

26
00:02:08.267 --> 00:02:11.702
Next, the warehouse. The vendor picks the warehouse called test.

27
00:02:20.267 --> 00:02:24.638
Stock quantity: one hundred bags. Minimum order quantity: ten bags.

28
00:02:24.638 --> 00:02:26.987
So a customer must buy at least ten.

29
00:02:32.267 --> 00:02:37.565
Product pricing comes from the master catalog. M R P four hundred thirty five

30
00:02:37.565 --> 00:02:43.275
Rupees, selling price three hundred ninety, and the tax type is exclusive of G S T.

31
00:02:56.267 --> 00:03:01.348
Now the optional price change request. The vendor asks for four hundred rupees,

32
00:03:01.348 --> 00:03:04.950
Because this is a metro city location with higher costs.

33
00:03:16.267 --> 00:03:20.235
A reason is required. The admin will see this reason when deciding.

34
00:03:24.267 --> 00:03:29.482
Below that, warranty and return policy. These also come from the master listing.

35
00:03:29.482 --> 00:03:34.827
The vendor can request a different warranty or return policy, again with a reason.

36
00:03:40.267 --> 00:03:43.705
At the bottom, allow cash on delivery for this listing.

37
00:03:43.705 --> 00:03:46.518
The vendor ticks it, and clicks Create S K U.

38
00:03:52.267 --> 00:03:57.672
The S K U is created. Stock goes up, and the new row shows the price request as

39
00:03:57.672 --> 00:03:58.219
Pending.

40
00:04:01.067 --> 00:04:05.610
Let's pause on the pricing part of the form, because this is where most confusion

41
00:04:05.610 --> 00:04:06.059
Happens.

42
00:04:06.509 --> 00:04:11.138
M R P, the maximum retail price, set by the admin in the catalog.

43
00:04:11.588 --> 00:04:14.991
Selling price, the price the customer actually pays.

44
00:04:14.991 --> 00:04:16.431
Also set by the admin.

45
00:04:16.881 --> 00:04:22.509
Tax type. Here it's exclusive of G S T, which means G S T is added on top of the

46
00:04:22.509 --> 00:04:23.494
Selling price.

47
00:04:23.944 --> 00:04:28.723
Requested price. Optional. Only fill this if the vendor needs a different price.

48
00:04:29.173 --> 00:04:32.160
And the reason, which is required with any request.

49
00:04:34.567 --> 00:04:37.148
Here are all the fields once more, in one place.

50
00:04:37.598 --> 00:04:42.692
The category filter shows only categories approved for this vendor during KYC.

51
00:04:42.692 --> 00:04:46.153
If a category is missing, the vendor must request it.

52
00:04:46.603 --> 00:04:49.610
The product always comes from the master catalog.

53
00:04:49.610 --> 00:04:53.046
If a product is missing, the admin must create it first.

54
00:04:53.496 --> 00:04:58.650
The warehouse is where the stock sits. The same product in two warehouses means two

55
00:04:58.650 --> 00:04:59.085
S K Us.

56
00:04:59.535 --> 00:05:03.951
Stock quantity must be honest. Customers can order whatever the app shows.

57
00:05:04.401 --> 00:05:08.501
Minimum order quantity stops tiny orders that aren't worth delivering.

58
00:05:08.501 --> 00:05:10.609
For bricks it might be five hundred.

59
00:05:11.059 --> 00:05:16.158
And allow C O D switches cash on delivery on or off, for this S K U only.

60
00:05:18.567 --> 00:05:21.127
A price request can be in one of three states.

61
00:05:21.577 --> 00:05:25.737
While it's pending, the S K U sells at the admin's catalog price.

62
00:05:25.737 --> 00:05:28.233
The vendor's new price is not live yet.

63
00:05:28.683 --> 00:05:32.694
If the admin accepts, the vendor's price goes live for that S K U.

64
00:05:33.144 --> 00:05:37.832
If the admin rejects, the price stays at the admin's price, for example three

65
00:05:37.832 --> 00:05:41.058
Hundred ninety rupees, and the status shows rejected.

66
00:05:43.467 --> 00:05:45.387
Let's watch this in the live demo.

67
00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:53.755
Now the admin side. From the admin panel, the admin opens Warehouses and Vendors.

68
00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:59.650
Every vendor is listed here. In the actions column, there's an icon for vendor

69
00:05:59.650 --> 00:06:00.645
Change requests.

70
00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:08.656
This vendor has no price requests, so the box is empty.

71
00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:18.363
The admin opens the right vendor.

72
00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:35.233
Here's the request. Current price three hundred ninety, requested price four

73
00:06:35.233 --> 00:06:37.157
Hundred, and the vendor's reason.

74
00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:41.783
There are two buttons: Reject and Accept price.

75
00:06:41.783 --> 00:06:43.941
The admin clicks Reject this time.

76
00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:55.770
Back on the vendor's inventory, the status now says rejected, and the price is back

77
00:06:55.770 --> 00:06:57.627
To three hundred ninety rupees.

78
00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:04.187
The same box has a second tab, for warranty and return policy requests.

79
00:07:04.637 --> 00:07:06.471
The price tab, which we just saw.

80
00:07:06.921 --> 00:07:08.777
And the warranty and return tab.

81
00:07:09.227 --> 00:07:14.181
It shows the requested warranty and the requested return policy, next to the current

82
00:07:14.181 --> 00:07:14.475
Ones.

83
00:07:14.925 --> 00:07:16.440
And the reason from the vendor.

84
00:07:16.890 --> 00:07:22.759
The admin can reject, or accept the policy. On accept, the new policy shows on that

85
00:07:22.759 --> 00:07:23.183
S K U.

86
00:07:25.600 --> 00:07:30.430
Remember this. A rejected price request does not stop the S K U from selling.

87
00:07:30.430 --> 00:07:33.629
It just keeps selling at the admin's catalog price.

88
00:07:33.629 --> 00:07:38.835
If the vendor still needs a change, they raise a new request with a clearer reason,

89
00:07:38.835 --> 00:07:41.344
Like higher transport cost in that city.

90
00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:27.120
Back to the inventory list. Each row tells the vendor a lot.

91
00:08:27.570 --> 00:08:29.917
The product name and its S K U code.

92
00:08:30.367 --> 00:08:32.372
The warehouse this stock belongs to.

93
00:08:32.822 --> 00:08:36.598
The price request status: accepted, pending or rejected.

94
00:08:37.048 --> 00:08:41.315
The stock level, and the status: in stock, low stock or out of stock.

95
00:08:41.765 --> 00:08:46.077
And on top, sync and export buttons. Sync refreshes the data.

96
00:08:46.077 --> 00:08:48.975
Export downloads the inventory as a file.

97
00:08:51.367 --> 00:08:53.756
These labels appear in the inventory list.

98
00:08:54.206 --> 00:08:56.382
In stock. There are enough units to sell.

99
00:08:56.832 --> 00:08:59.392
Low stock. It's running out. Restock soon.

100
00:08:59.842 --> 00:09:04.045
Out of stock. Zero units. Customers cannot order this S K U.

101
00:09:04.495 --> 00:09:07.866
Price pending. A price request is waiting for the admin.

102
00:09:08.316 --> 00:09:12.604
Rejected. The request was rejected, so it sells at the admin's price.

103
00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:18.477
Here are the mistakes vendors make most often in inventory.

104
00:09:18.927 --> 00:09:22.917
Entering stock they don't really have. That leads to cancelled orders.

105
00:09:23.367 --> 00:09:27.335
A price request with no clear reason. It will likely be rejected.

106
00:09:27.785 --> 00:09:30.835
The wrong warehouse. Then pickup goes to the wrong place.

107
00:09:31.285 --> 00:09:35.424
Forgetting the minimum order quantity, so customers place tiny orders.

108
00:09:35.874 --> 00:09:39.351
And expecting a change to be live before the admin approves it.

109
00:09:41.767 --> 00:09:45.120
Quick check. The admin's price is three hundred ninety.

110
00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:48.840
The vendor requested four hundred, and the admin rejected it.

111
00:09:48.840 --> 00:09:51.644
What do customers pay now? Think for a moment.

112
00:09:55.594 --> 00:10:00.632
The answer: three hundred ninety rupees. A rejected request falls back to the

113
00:10:00.632 --> 00:10:03.445
Admin's price, and the S K U keeps selling.

114
00:10:06.233 --> 00:10:07.940
Let's summarise module two.

115
00:10:08.390 --> 00:10:13.126
Add S K U means category, product, warehouse, stock and minimum quantity.

116
00:10:13.576 --> 00:10:17.650
Price, warranty and return policy come from the master catalog.

117
00:10:18.100 --> 00:10:20.170
Any change request needs a reason.

118
00:10:20.620 --> 00:10:24.118
The admin accepts or rejects it in vendor change requests.

119
00:10:24.568 --> 00:10:29.900
And rejected means back to the admin's price. Next, in module three, warehouses and

120
00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:30.350
Pickup.

121
00:10:32.767 --> 00:10:38.484
That's the end of module 2. Next up, module 3: Warehouses and pickup verification.
